Z||000001||DJRice||07-21-2000||09:24 AM||||If the radiator is hot on top and cool on the bottom, replace it because its clogged.  Flush the system out while your at it.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||07-21-2000||01:05 PM||||<BR>Isn't a properly functioning radiator hotter on the top than it is on the bottom? The hot water from the engine goes in at the top, gets cooled in the radiator, and then comes out the bottom. Am I wrong?||||reg||5
Z||000003||StuGood||07-21-2000||01:10 PM||||Sounds like radiator plugosis - crud settles to bottom of radiator and plugs the bottom passages first.  At least, that's what I envision.  If it doesn't leak, it might be less expensive to have it reconditioned ("if it isn't rotted out, rod it out.").  <P>Patrick: Stock Fieros have a <B>cross-flow</B> radiator (not top-to-bottom flow), with tanks on the sides. So temperature gradient would tend be horizontal instead of vertical    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . <P>There's probably <B>some</B> vertical temperature gradient, too, because of convection in the tanks, but the most noticeable one would be horizontal, due to  the radiator removing heat as the coolant flows across.   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-21-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000004||Patrick||07-21-2000||03:34 PM||||<BR>Tanks Stu <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, I stand corrected.||||reg||14
Z||000005||rockcrawl||07-21-2000||04:17 PM||||This post reminds me of when I was working on one of my cars over a period of two years. I had the radiator hoses off, and the coolant tubes open. Well I guess Mickey thought the antifreeze in the tubes tasted good, so he soaked his corn in it! The stupid mouse had the tubes filled with corn and I didn't realize it until it ended up in the radiator! Just a reminder, If you leave your project sit with the hoses off, plug the holes with rags, or Mick will get in there!<P>Jon <P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||12
Z||000006||StuGood||07-21-2000||07:38 PM||||Glad somebody else beat me to the corny pun this time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !||||reg||10
Z||000007||bcibob670||07-21-2000||09:42 PM||||Thank you all for your assistance. <P>the cookie goes to the plugged up radiator  <BR>I got a junker and had it flow tested etc and replaced the one i had in the car .<P>i have taken the car out and the cooling is just fine...<P>THANKS ALL <BR>||||reg||1
